{"id":9018,"date":"2024-08-05T07:00:00","date_gmt":"2024-08-05T07:00:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/?p=9018"},"modified":"2025-09-04T23:14:20","modified_gmt":"2025-09-04T23:14:20","slug":"how-to-build-an-adu-on-my-existing-home","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/how-to-build-an-adu-on-my-existing-home\/","title":{"rendered":"How To Build An ADU On My Existing Home?"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">&#8220;<em>How To Build An ADU On My Existing Home?<\/em>&#8220;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><br>Accessory Dwelling Units (ADUs) are an increasingly popular choice for homeowners aiming to maximize their property&#8217;s potential. Whether you&#8217;re seeking additional rental income, a comfortable space for a family member, or an expansion of your living area, an ADU can significantly enhance your home&#8217;s functionality and value. In this comprehensive guide, we&#8217;ll walk you through everything you need to know about building an ADU on your existing property, from the initial planning stages to the final construction. And remember, <a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/\" title=\"\">Harris &amp; Sons<\/a> is here to turn your ADU vision into reality. Read on to discover how we can help you create the perfect addition to your home, seamlessly and professionally.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/05\/accessory-dwelling-unit.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-9021\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What is an ADU?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">An ADU, or Accessory Dwelling Unit, is a secondary housing unit on a single-family residential lot. ADUs come in various forms, including detached units, garage conversions, basement apartments, or additions to the existing structure. They typically include all the amenities of a small home, such as a kitchen, bathroom, and living space.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why Build an ADU?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Building an ADU offers numerous benefits:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Increased Property Value<\/strong>: Adding an ADU can significantly boost the resale value of your home.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Additional Income<\/strong>: Rent out the ADU for extra monthly income.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Multigenerational Living<\/strong>: Provide a comfortable living space for aging parents or adult children.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Flexible Use<\/strong>: Use the ADU as a guest house, home office, or personal retreat.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Steps to Construct an ADU<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">1. Check Local Regulations and Zoning Laws<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Before you begin planning your ADU, it\u2019s crucial to understand the legal requirements in your area. Your ability to build an ADU is subject to state and city zoning, ordinances, and building codes. For example, in regions like Bend, OR, and Tigard, OR, specific regulations may dictate the size, placement, and design of your ADU.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Zoning Laws<\/strong>: Verify that your property is zoned for an ADU.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Building Codes<\/strong>: Ensure that your plans comply with local building codes.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Permits<\/strong>: Obtain the necessary permits from your local building department.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">2. Plan Your ADU Project<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Once you have a clear understanding of the legal requirements, the next step is to plan your ADU project. This involves deciding on the type of ADU you want to build and how it will be used.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Type of ADU<\/strong>: Decide between a detached unit, garage conversion, basement apartment, or addition.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Purpose<\/strong>: Determine if the ADU will be used for rental income, housing a family member, or another purpose.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Design and Layout<\/strong>: Create a floor plan that maximizes space efficiency and meets your needs.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">3. Designing Your ADU<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Designing an ADU requires careful consideration of space, functionality, and aesthetics. Working with an architect or designer can help ensure that your ADU is both practical and visually appealing.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Space-Efficient Designs<\/strong>: Opt for designs that make the most of limited space.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Custom ADU Design<\/strong>: Tailor the design to match your existing home\u2019s style and layout.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>ADU Floor Plans<\/strong>: Develop detailed floor plans that include all necessary features.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">4. Budgeting and Financing<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Building an ADU is a significant financial investment. It\u2019s essential to create a budget and explore financing options to ensure you can cover the costs.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Cost Estimates<\/strong>: Obtain cost estimates for materials, labor, permits, and other expenses.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Financing Options<\/strong>: Consider home equity loans, personal savings, or other financing methods.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Budget Planning<\/strong>: Create a detailed budget to track your expenses throughout the project.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">5. Obtaining Permits<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Navigating the permit process can be complex, but it\u2019s a critical step in building your ADU. Each locality has specific requirements, so it\u2019s essential to understand and follow the process.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Building Permits<\/strong>: Submit your ADU plans to the local building department for approval.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Zoning Permits<\/strong>: Ensure your project complies with zoning regulations.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Inspections<\/strong>: Schedule inspections at various stages of construction to ensure compliance.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/05\/Multi-Family-ADU-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-9022\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">6. Hiring Contractors<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Hiring experienced contractors can make a significant difference in the quality and efficiency of your ADU construction. Look for professionals with experience in building ADUs and a strong reputation.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Selecting Contractors<\/strong>: Interview multiple contractors and check references.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Contract Agreements<\/strong>: Ensure you have detailed contracts outlining the scope of work, timelines, and costs.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Project Management<\/strong>: Maintain regular communication with your contractors to keep the project on track.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/\" title=\"\">Harris &amp; Sons<\/a> has extensive professional experience and an outstanding reputation in ADU construction. We are ready for interviews and eager to cooperate with you to bring your vision to life. <a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/contact-us-2\/\" title=\"\">Call us today<\/a>, and let&#8217;s start making our grand plans a reality.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">7. Construction Phase<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The construction phase involves transforming your plans into reality. This stage includes site preparation, building the structure, installing utilities, and finishing work.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Site Preparation<\/strong>: Clear and prepare the site for construction.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Building the Structure<\/strong>: Construct the ADU according to the approved plans.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Installing Utilities<\/strong>: Ensure that plumbing, electrical, and HVAC systems are properly installed.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Finishing Work<\/strong>: Complete interior and exterior finishes, such as painting, flooring, and landscaping.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">8. Final Inspections and Approvals<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">After construction is complete, you\u2019ll need to pass final inspections to ensure that your ADU meets all building codes and regulations.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Final Inspections<\/strong>: Schedule inspections with local authorities.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Certificate of Occupancy<\/strong>: Obtain a certificate of occupancy, allowing the ADU to be legally inhabited.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Financial Considerations<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Building an ADU can be a profitable investment, but it\u2019s important to consider the financial implications carefully.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Financing Your ADU<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">There are several financing options available for building an ADU, including:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Home Equity Loans<\/strong>: Borrow against the equity in your home to finance the ADU construction.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Construction Loans<\/strong>: Obtain a loan specifically for the construction project.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Personal Savings<\/strong>: Use personal savings to fund the project.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Budget Planning<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Create a detailed budget that includes all potential expenses, such as:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Construction Costs<\/strong>: Materials, labor, permits, and inspections.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Design Fees<\/strong>: Architect or designer fees.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Utility Installation<\/strong>: Plumbing, electrical, and HVAC systems.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Finishing Costs<\/strong>: Interior and exterior finishes, landscaping.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Long-Term Financial Benefits<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Investing in an ADU can provide long-term financial benefits, including:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Rental Income<\/strong>: Generate additional income by renting out the ADU.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Increased Property Value<\/strong>: Enhance the resale value of your home.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Mortgage Offset<\/strong>: Use rental income to help pay off your mortgage.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/05\/05_1-Photo-1024x619-1.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-9020\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Legal and Logistical Considerations<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Understanding the legal and logistical aspects of building an ADU is crucial to avoid potential issues and ensure a smooth project.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Legal Requirements<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Zoning Laws<\/strong>: Verify that your property is zoned for an ADU.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Building Codes<\/strong>: Ensure your ADU complies with local building codes.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Permits<\/strong>: Obtain all necessary permits before starting construction.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Logistical Considerations<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Site Access<\/strong>: Ensure there is adequate access to the construction site.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Utility Connections<\/strong>: Plan for connections to existing utilities, such as water, sewer, and electricity.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Parking<\/strong>: Consider parking requirements for the new unit.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Conclusion<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Building an ADU on your existing property is a rewarding project that can significantly enhance your home\u2019s functionality and value. By carefully planning, budgeting, and adhering to local regulations, you can successfully add an ADU to your property.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">At <a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/\" title=\"\">Harris &amp; Sons<\/a>, we specialize in designing and constructing ADUs, ensuring that every aspect of the project is handled with professionalism and expertise. From initial planning to final construction, we remove the complexities and challenges, allowing you to focus on the exciting aspects of your new addition. For homeowners in Oregon and Portland <a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/contact-us-2\/\" title=\"\">contact us today<\/a> for a free property appraisal and consultation. Let <a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/\" title=\"\">Harris &amp; Sons<\/a> bring your ADU vision to life seamlessly and efficiently.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>&#8220;How To Build An ADU On My Existing Home?&#8220; Accessory Dwelling Units (ADUs) are an increasingly popular choice for homeowners aiming to maximize their property&#8217;s potential. Whether you&#8217;re seeking additional rental income, a comfortable space for a family member, or an expansion of your living area, an ADU can significantly enhance your home&#8217;s functionality and [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":9023,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[34],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-9018","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-addition-resources"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/9018","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=9018"}],"version-history":[{"count":3,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/9018\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":13484,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/9018\/revisions\/13484"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=9018"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=9018"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=9018"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}